[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3496080463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112459#issuecomment-3496080463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112459","id":3496080463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QYfRP","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T09:17:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T09:20:22Z","body":"The behavior of using `OP_NOT_EQUAL` has been used since at least 2016. I assume it was thought that using separate operators for `==` and `!=` would somehow be beneficial. Otherwise, we wouldn't have a separate `OP_NOT_EQUAL` in the first place.\r\n\r\nBy not calling `OP_NOT_EQUAL` here, we'd be making a first step towards \"deprecating\" `OP_NOT_EQUAL` altogether, by not calling it from our own `!=` operations. I think this is good, but it should be discussed.\r\n\r\nThe comment was added in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/35816, cc @touilleMan ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3496080463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3915312053","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112459#issuecomment-3915312053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112459","id":3915312053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pXuu1","user":{"login":"touilleMan","id":3187637,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODc2Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3187637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan","html_url":"https://github.com/touilleMan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T15:16:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T15:16:06Z","body":"> The comment was added in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/35816, cc @touilleMan\r\n\r\nMy memory is ~totally crumbling~ imperfect, but I think my rational here was to consider the `OP_NOT_EQUAL` operator similarly to [Python `__ne__`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/operator.html#operator.__ne__). So in theory a object could overwrite how `OP_NOT_EQUAL` was working, and then `my_custom_obj1 != my_custom_obj2` would behave differently from `[my_custom_obj1] != [my_custom_obj2]`\r\n\r\nHowever, like @Ivorforce say, this is something that haven't materialized in the end. And I'm 100% favorable to remove `OP_NOT_EQUAL` and consider `!=` is always the invert of `==` :+1: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3915312053/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]